---
/* Plan Q13 (a, owner's choice for now): a project-only page. A named
   founder story can replace the "Who" section once the owner writes it. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import CtaClose from "../components/CtaClose.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { REPO_URL } from "../config";
---

<Base
  title="About Rulebox"
  description="Why Rulebox exists, how it is built, and how the project is run: an open-source kiosk OS for the Windows PCs that staff share."
  path="/about"
  og="about"
  crumbs={[{ name: "About", path: "/about" }]}
>
  <PageHero label="About" title="A small project for a common problem." sub="Every workplace has a PC that everyone shares and nobody owns. Rulebox exists to make that PC do its job, and nothing else." tone="sun" />

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container cols">
      <div class="prose flush">
        <h2>Why it exists</h2>
        <p>Shared PCs go wrong slowly. Someone installs a game, someone saves their passwords in the browser, someone clicks a link in an email. The usual fixes are stickers, Windows' own kiosk mode, or a device-management suite that does a hundred things. A shop with six PCs does not have an IT department. It has a person who is "good with computers".</p>
        <p>Rulebox is for that person. Install one small program, type a code, and the PC becomes a locked, branded workstation that you manage from a web page.</p>
        <h2>How it is built</h2>
        <p>A Rust service on the PC, a friendly desktop for staff, and a web dashboard. Desired state, not commands: every change is versioned and signed, and a PC that was offline simply moves to the latest version. Every installer is hash-checked before it runs.</p>
        <h2>How the project is run</h2>
        <p>In the open, under the MIT licence. The roadmap, the changelog and the known limits are public. We publish no numbers without a source, and no customer names without written permission.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="side" aria-label="More about Rulebox">
        <ul class="icon-list" role="list">
          <li data-tone="mint">
            <span class="il-icon"><Icon name="code" /></span>
            <span class="il-text"><a class="il-a" href={REPO_URL}>The code</a><span class="muted">Read it on GitHub</span></span>
          </li>
          <li data-tone="violet">
            <span class="il-icon"><Icon name="signpost" /></span>
            <span class="il-text"><a class="il-a" href="/roadmap">The roadmap</a><span class="muted">Built, next, later, not planned</span></span>
          </li>
          <li data-tone="coral">
            <span class="il-icon"><Icon name="shield" /></span>
            <span class="il-text"><a class="il-a" href="/security">The security design</a><span class="muted">And its limits</span></span>
          </li>
          <li data-tone="blue">
            <span class="il-icon"><Icon name="letter" /></span>
            <span class="il-text"><a class="il-a" href="/contact">Contact</a><span class="muted">We reply by email</span></span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaClose />
</Base>

<style>
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sp-8);
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--sp-10);
    }
  }
</style>
